id: E543-draft-DBC4
trigger_tool: Conan|Rakudo|Raku|OHOS runtime|test_package
phase: testing|packaging
error_signature: "Error loading shared library libmoar.so|Cannot find Log in:|Perl 6/Raku 6.d module executed with Perl 5|Your printf-style directives specify 0 arguments"
severity: 2
category: runtime, dependency, conan, testing
match_keywords: Raku, Rakudo, MoarVM, libmoar.so, RAKULIB, OHOS, HarmonyOS, KERNEL.name, harmonyos, Str.fmt, template dispatch
prescan_pattern: '\.rakumod$|"perl"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*"6\.d"'
title: Raku module packaging and runtime environment on OHOS
root_cause: Raku 6.d modules require Rakudo and its MoarVM runtime; the Perl 5 executable is not compatible. The Rakudo package's bin/raku dynamically loads libmoar.so from its package lib directory, and module discovery requires RAKULIB to point at the packaged module tree. On OHOS the MoarVM port reports $*KERNEL.name as "harmonyos" and a HongMeng kernel release, whereas Linux reports "linux" - this is the reliable way to bind a test to the OHOS target. Separately, Raku's Str.fmt treats its first positional argument as the format string, so role methods that delegate template dispatch via $template.fmt(|@args) do not provide sprintf semantics and die at runtime.
affected_scope: Pure Raku modules packaged with Conan for HarmonyOS PC aarch64 using the published Rakudo runtime.
verification_cmd: "conan create archives/r/raku-log/0.3.1 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 --build=raku-log/*"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: use-published-rakudo-and-export-runtime-paths
rec_description: Declare a pinned published rakudo runtime dependency, package pure Raku modules without a fake native build step, set RAKULIB to the package module directory, add the Rakudo package lib directory to LD_LIBRARY_PATH, and disable MoarVM JIT for HarmonyOS execution. For OHOS-specific tests assert on $*KERNEL.name eq 'harmonyos' (Linux reports 'linux'), which genuinely fails off-target. Declare only os/arch settings when nothing is compiled. Do not assert on Raku template dispatch that relies on Str.fmt with caller-supplied arguments.
rec_command: "self.requires(\"rakudo/2025.11\", run=True); env[\"RAKULIB\"] = module_dir; env[\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\"] = rakudo_lib + os.pathsep + env.get(\"LD_LIBRARY_PATH\", \"\"); env[\"MVM_JIT_DISABLE\"] = \"1\"; is $*KERNEL.name, 'harmonyos'"
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: recipe-edit
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: inspect-runtime-package-layout
fallback_description: If a different Rakudo revision uses another runtime library or site module path, inspect its package layout and run a minimal module import before changing Conan environment metadata. Probe `raku -e 'say $*KERNEL.name'` on the target to confirm what the port reports before writing platform assertions.
fallback_command: "find $RAKUDO_PACKAGE -name 'libmoar.so*' -o -name raku; raku -I $MODULE_DIR -e 'use Log'; raku -e 'say $*KERNEL.name'"
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: manual
forbid_1_pattern: "use Perl 5 as a Raku runtime|LD_LIBRARY_PATH=.*SYS_PREFIX|echo.*raku-log"
forbid_1_reason: Perl 5 cannot execute Raku modules, shared global prefix injection is not reproducible, and print-only package tests do not exercise the module API.
forbid_1_consequence: The consumer cannot load the Raku runtime or module in a clean Conan environment.
forbid_2_pattern: '\$[A-Za-z0-9:_-]+\.fmt\(\|@args\)'
forbid_2_reason: Raku's Str.fmt takes its first positional argument as the format string, so template dispatch written as $template.fmt(|@args) does not provide sprintf semantics and raises "Your printf-style directives specify 0 arguments, but 1 argument was supplied". Assertions that depend on this path fail; use sprintf semantics or the single-argument method when testing formatting.
forbid_2_consequence: A test or consumer relying on this delegation dies at runtime on every platform, including OHOS.
principles: P003, P018
